Table 2 shows the association of weight loss with 3-year changes in traditional lipid biomarkers. Compared to people who did not lose weight (i.e., weight gain), those with 5–10% and >10% weight loss significantly improved levels of HDL and decreased triglycerides at the year 3 visit (i.e., study exit). In addition, LDL cholesterol levels decreased in individuals with >10% weight loss compared to those who did not lose weight. Specifically, levels of LDL cholesterol decreased by 8.3% (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
