Table 3 shows the association of weight loss with 3-year changes in biomarkers of inflammation. Compared to people who did not lose weight, those with 5–10% and >10% weight loss had lower levels of hs-CRP, hs-IL6, and higher levels of adiponectin hormone at the year 3 visit (i.e., study exit). People with >10% weight loss also decreased levels of GlycA. Specifically, compared to individuals who did not lose weight, individuals with more than 10% weight loss had a decrease in levels of hs-CRP by 59.5% (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
